  "body": "Part of #5610 — implements item 1 of the fix-packet spec recorded on that issue (re-triage, task 12232): the provider retirement gate.\n\n## What this adds\n\n- `scripts/check-provider-retirement-gate.sh` — the retirement gate. Given a provider id, it greps the repo `.opencode/opencode.jsonc`, the deployed `~/.config/opencode/opencode.jsonc`, the `~/.local/share/opencode/opencode.jsonc` copy, and the runtime-state config (or explicit `--config` files) and exits **1 (retirement BLOCKED)** while any active reference remains, **0** when zero references remain, **2** on usage/no-config errors (`--allow-empty` overrides the last).\n- `scripts/tests/test_check_provider_retirement_gate.py` — 7 contract tests (positive: references present → blocked; negative: no references → pass; explicit-config, missing-config, and usage cases). All 7 pass.\n- Wiring references so the gate is found at retirement time: a pointer block at the end of `.github/scripts/check-proxy-port-fallbacks.sh` and in the retirement note in `home/common/default.nix`.\n\n## Verification (live, on the laptop, 2026-11-08)\n\n- `scripts/check-provider-retirement-gate.sh opencode-route` → exit 1 (40 references in the deployed config and 40 in the repo config — retirement correctly blocked today).\n- `scripts/check-provider-retirement-gate.sh no-such-provider-xyz` → exit 0.\n- Contract tests: 7/7 pass, before and after rebasing onto current `main`.\n\n## Provenance / remaining scope on #5610\n\nThe gate commit was originally authored by lane code-k (commit ae96f39a44) in this task's worktree but never pushed or PR'd; this shift (task 13040, lane code-h) verified it, rebased it onto current main (b3be8d4c02), re-ran the tests, and opened this PR.\n\nNot in this PR, still tracked on #5610: the interim-state resolution is proceeding under #5768 (deploy-registry entry merged in PR #7631; activation waits on the systemd renderer slice and #7641), and the #3232 receipt-validation audit remains owed. This PR does not close #5610.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796732202&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7679&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7679&signature=d4b5d85f28ef5a57e0eb58794977b87e6ce74666460070efb4328e7e1614580f\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7679?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **New Features**\n  * Added a provider retirement check that scans selected or discovered configuration files for active references. It ignores comments and disabled-provider entries, and can allow runs with no configuration files found.\n* **Documentation**\n  * Added guidance to run the retirement check and verify that no active configuration references remain before retiring a provider.\n* **Tests**\n  * Added coverage for matching and clean configurations, provider identity, comments, disabled entries, missing or unreadable files, and empty configuration sets.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
